course: dictionary
lesson: 3181
title: Enclave: a place inside a place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An enclave is a small area that is completely surrounded by somewhere else. Picture a jam doughnut: the jam is inside, and the dough is all around it. The clue is in the words «a piece of one country completely surrounded by another».
explain: «In the town of Baarle, the border between Belgium and the Netherlands weaves through streets and even houses, making dozens of tiny enclaves.» The clues are tiny, weaves and surrounded. Try the swap: "making dozens of tiny small areas surrounded by something else" still makes sense, so enclave must mean a small area cut off inside something bigger.
explain: Enclave can also describe people. A cultural enclave is a neighbourhood where a group of people live together, apart from others, often sharing one language. The same word can describe a country, a street or a community, so always check the sentence for clues.
fact: An enclave is a small piece of land completely surrounded by another country.
fact: «Lesotho» is an enclave inside South Africa.
fact: «San Marino» and «Vatican City» are both enclaves inside Italy.
fact: «Enclave» can also mean a part of a town where a particular group of people live together, apart from others.
fact: Enclave can mean any small area that is different from everything around it.
exercise: Lesotho is an enclave inside which country? | Italy | *South Africa | Belgium | Botswana
exercise: Find and copy one word from «making dozens of tiny enclaves» that means very small. | enclaves | *tiny | making | dozens
exercise: What is a «cultural enclave»? | *A neighbourhood where a group of people live together, apart from others | A ship that sails around the world | A tall tower in a busy city | A type of weather
test: San Marino and Vatican City are enclaves inside which country? | *Italy | Spain | Greece | France
test: Nadia says an enclave is just an island. What is the difference? | An enclave is in the sea, but an island is on land | *An island is surrounded by water, but an enclave is surrounded by land of another country | Islands and enclaves mean exactly the same thing
exam: Which best describes an enclave? | *A small area surrounded by a different country or place | A large ocean with many islands | A type of rain | A very fast train
